const rawSourceContent = "Key Takeaways\r\nUnderstanding Mind-Body Health & Wellbeing\r\nEmotional Stress & Physical Health Connection\r\nBrain, Nervous System & Stress Response\r\nGut-Brain Axis & Digestive Health\r\nStress, IBS & Acidity\r\nStress, Headaches & Migraine\r\nStress & High Blood Pressure\r\nStress & Thyroid Health\r\nFatigue, Sleep & Energy Levels\r\nSigns Stress May Affect Physical Health\r\nWhen Physical Symptoms Need Medical Evaluation\r\nHealthy Lifestyle & Stress Management\r\nMind-Body Health Assessment Process\r\nNeuro-Ayurveda Development System\r\nPersonalised Mind-Body Wellbeing Support\r\nFAQs About Mind-Body Health\r\n\r\nMind-Body Health Care & Stress-Related Health\r\n\r\n\r\nUnderstanding the Connection Between Emotional Wellbeing, Brain Health and Physical Health\r\n\r\nThe mind and body constantly communicate with each other. Emotional stress doesn't just impact thoughts and feelings, it can impact physical well-being as well. Emotional wellbeing, mood and quality of life are also affected by long-term physical health issues, similarly. [1][2]\r\n\r\nMany folks find that they get digestive discomfort, acidosis, headaches, migraine, tiredness, sleep disturbances, muscle tension or blood pressure issues during times of prolonged stress or anxiety. Others may have exacerbation of their medical problems when they are under emotional stress. [1][2]\r\n\r\nThis is not to say that all the physical symptoms are due to stress. It is important to always assess physical health issues properly by a qualified health care provider. But studies have proved that emotional health and physical health go hand in hand and they interact with each other in complex ways, through the brain, nervous system, hormones, immune system and via a connection between the gut and the brain. [1][4][9]\r\n\r\nWe recognise at Manovaidya that supporting emotional wellbeing is an important aspect of understanding overall health. We don't think of the mind and body as distinct, but rather how emotional, lifestyle and biological factors combine to affect wellbeing.\r\n\r\nDr. Ankush Garg, Mental Health Specialist and Founder of Manovaidya, who leads us, follow the Neuro-Ayurveda Development System which is a five pillar system that takes a holistic approach to brain, gut, behaviour, lifestyle and emotional wellbeing and supports long-term mind-body wellness.\r\n\r\nMind-Body Health Conditions We Support\r\n\r\nStress and emotional wellbeing can have an impact on various systems of the body in different people. At our Mind-Body Health Care we want to grasp the link between emotional health and prevalent physical issues that are caused by stress.\r\n\r\n\r\nStress & Digestive Health\r\n\r\nA knowledge of the possible effect of stress on digestion, appetite, bloating and general digestive health. [4][10]\r\n\r\nLearn More → Stress & Digestive Health\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nStress & IBS\r\n\r\nAssisting the person to understand how emotional stress relates to Irritable Bowel Syndrome (IBS). [3][10]\r\n\r\nLearn More → Stress & IBS\r\n\r\n\r\nStress & Acidity\r\n\r\nKnowing about the relationship between acid reflux, indigestion and stomach discomfort with emotional stress. [10]\r\n\r\nLearn More → Stress & Acidity\r\n\r\n\r\nStress & Migraine\r\n\r\nExploring how stress may act as a trigger for migraine episodes in some individuals. [6]\r\n\r\nLearn More → Stress & Migraine\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nStress & Headaches\r\n\r\nTo recognise tension headaches and how emotional wellbeing may contribute to the pathway of headaches. [1]\r\n\r\nHow to stress-free and headache-free.Learn how to reduce stress and headaches.\r\n\r\n\r\nStress & High Blood Pressure\r\n\r\nUnderstanding the relationship between chronic stress and blood pressure as well as other medical and lifestyle factors. [1][5]\r\n\r\nFind out more about stress & high blood pressure.\r\n\r\n\r\nStress & Thyroid Health\r\n\r\nGaining an understanding of how stress, emotional wellbeing and living with thyroid disorders are related and that thyroid disorders are a medical diagnosis and must be managed.\r\n\r\nLearn More → Stress & Thyroid Health\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nStress & Fatigue\r\n\r\nRecognising a sense of tiredness, emotional exhaustion, and appreciating how stress, sleep and lifestyle can affect well-being. [1][2]\r\n\r\nLearn More → Stress & Fatigue\r\n\r\n\r\nWhy Mind-Body Health Matters\r\n\r\nThere are several biological systems which link the brain and the body in a constant relationship. [1][9]\r\n\r\nEmotional wellbeing may influence:\r\n\r\n•\tSleep quality\r\n•\tDigestion\r\n•\tAppetite\r\n•\tEnergy levels\r\n•\tMuscle tension\r\n•\tPain perception\r\n•\tHeart rate\r\n•\tStress hormone regulation\r\n•\tOverall quality of life\r\n\r\nLikewise, chronic physical illness can also have an impact on emotional health, stress and functioning. [1][2]\r\n\r\nUnderstanding of this two-way relationship helps the healthcare professional to see the whole person, not just the symptoms.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nUnderstanding the Mind-Body Connection\r\n\r\nMind and body are not distinct systems. They communicate with each other, all the time, via the brain, nervous system, hormones, and immune system and gut-brain axis. This close connection means that emotional wellbeing can have a negative impact on physical health and vice versa. [1][4][9]\r\n\r\nFor instance, many people have complained of experiencing stomach ache before an important meeting, headaches at a critical moment or disturbed sleep when they are under too much stress. Likewise, having a long-term physical health condition can be a source of emotional stress, anxiety or low mood. [1][2][10]\r\n\r\nIt is important to recognise this bi-directional relationship to look beyond the symptoms at a time and value emotional and physical wellbeing.\r\n\r\nRemember, not all the physical symptoms are due to stress. If any symptoms last or are severe, any underlying medical conditions should be evaluated by an appropriate health care professional at all times.\r\n\r\n________________________________________\r\n\r\nHow Stress Can Affect Different Body Systems\r\n\r\nWhen we are stressed, we enter into the natural stress response system which helps us to deal with difficult situations. Stress is a normal and healthy reaction when it arises for a short time. When stress persists for prolonged periods, however, it could impact several body systems. [1][2]\r\n\r\nBrain & Nervous System\r\n\r\nChronic emotional stress may influence:\r\n\r\n•\tConcentration\r\n•\tMemory\r\n•\tSleep quality\r\n•\tEmotional regulation\r\n•\tMental fatigue\r\n•\tDecision-making\r\n\r\nStress also can make coping with daily demands more difficult. [1][2]\r\n\r\n\r\nDigestive System\r\n\r\nThe gut and brain are constantly in communication via the gut-brain axis. [4][9]\r\n\r\nFor some, symptoms of the digestive system get worse when they are emotionally stressed, for example:\r\n\r\n•\tChanges in appetite\r\n•\tBloating\r\n•\tIndigestion\r\n•\tAbdominal discomfort\r\n•\tChanges in bowel habits\r\n\r\nIf symptoms of the digestive system persist, they should always be assessed by a competent health care practitioner. [3][10]\r\n\r\n→ Learn More About Stress & Digestive Health\r\n\r\n________________________________________\r\n\r\nCardiovascular System\r\n\r\nStress can acutely affect blood pressure and heart rate as a normal stress response. [1]\r\n\r\nMany factors affect long term cardiovascular health: [5]\r\n\r\n•\tAge\r\n•\tGenetics\r\n•\tDiet\r\n•\tPhysical activity\r\n•\tMedical conditions\r\n•\tLifestyle habits\r\n\r\nCare for emotional wellbeing can help with overall cardiovascular health as part of a healthy lifestyle. [1][5]\r\n\r\nStretching is a helpful exercise for reducing stress.Stretch is a valuable exercise to help lower stress.\r\n\r\n\r\nHormonal System\r\n\r\nMany other hormonal systems are affected by the stress hormones. [1]\r\n\r\nSome people will experience emotional stress in the following areas:\r\n\r\n•\tSleep\r\n•\tEnergy\r\n•\tAppetite\r\n•\tEmotional balance\r\n\r\nThe hormonal situation must always be assessed and treated by a trained health-care professional.\r\n\r\n→ Learn More About Stress & Thyroid Health\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nMuscles & Pain\r\n\r\nSome people tend to have tighter muscles if they are stressed emotionally. [1]\r\n\r\nIt can manifest itself as:\r\n\r\n•\tNeck stiffness\r\n•\tShoulder tension\r\n•\tJaw tightness\r\n•\tTension headaches\r\n•\tGeneral body discomfort\r\n\r\nSome people may find that muscle tension can be reduced by healthy coping and relaxation techniques. [1][2]\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nSleep\r\n\r\nStress can affect sleep and sleep can affect stress. [1][2]\r\n\r\nLack of sleep can lead to emotional stress and chronic emotional stress can make it more difficult to fall asleep and/or stay asleep.\r\n\r\nHealthy sleep supports:\r\n\r\n•\tBrain function\r\n•\tEmotional regulation\r\n•\tPhysical recovery\r\n•\tEnergy levels\r\n•\tOverall wellbeing\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nCommon Signs That Stress May Be Affecting Physical Health\r\n\r\nEach person has a unique reaction to emotional stress.\r\n\r\nSome individuals get just emotional symptoms, and others experience physical changes. [1][2]\r\n\r\nPossible signs include:\r\n\r\nDigestive Changes\r\n\r\n•\tFrequent indigestion\r\n•\tBloating\r\n•\tAcidity\r\n•\tStomach discomfort\r\n•\tChanges in bowel habits\r\n\r\nHead & Neck\r\n\r\n•\tFrequent headaches\r\n•\tMigraine triggers\r\n•\tNeck stiffness\r\n•\tJaw tension\r\n\r\nEnergy Levels\r\n\r\n•\tConstant tiredness\r\n•\tReduced motivation\r\n•\tFeeling physically exhausted\r\n•\tDifficulty recovering after rest\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nSleep\r\n\r\n•\tDifficulty falling asleep\r\n•\tFrequent waking\r\n•\tRestless sleep\r\n•\tDifficulty staying awake while awake\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nEmotional Changes\r\n\r\n•\tIncreased worrying\r\n•\tIrritability\r\n•\tDifficulty relaxing\r\n•\tFeeling emotionally overwhelmed\r\n\r\nThese symptoms also do not occur only because of stress. It is crucial to have a thorough medical evaluation to determine their causes.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nWhen Should Physical Symptoms Be Medically Evaluated?\r\n\r\nStress can impact on physical health but should not be assumed to be the only cause of any physical symptoms.\r\n\r\nYou should seek appropriate medical evaluation if you experience:\r\n\r\n•\tPersistent or worsening symptoms\r\n•\tSevere pain\r\n•\tBlood in stool or vomit\r\n•\tSudden chest pain\r\n•\tDifficulty breathing\r\n•\tUnexplained weight loss\r\n•\tFainting\r\n•\tHigh fever\r\n•\tSudden neurological symptoms\r\n\r\nMedical emergencies need to be attended to immediately.\r\n\r\nEmotional wellbeing and lifestyle may also be a factor in the care offered following appropriate medical evaluation if relevant.\r\n\r\n\r\nSupporting Mind-Body Health\r\n\r\nIt takes a holistic approach to care to support emotional and physical wellbeing, rather than just one symptom.\r\n\r\nSome overall healthy habits that can help the mind-body wellbeing are: [2]\r\n\r\n•\tRegular physical activity\r\n•\tHealthy sleep\r\n•\tBalanced nutrition\r\n•\tStress management\r\n•\tMindfulness and relaxation practices\r\n•\tHealthy social relationships\r\n•\tLimiting tobacco and excessive alcohol use\r\n•\tFollowing medical advice for existing health conditions\r\n•\tSeeking professional support when emotional or physical concerns persist\r\n\r\nAt Manovaidya, we believe that understanding the connection between emotional wellbeing and physical health helps individuals take a more balanced approach towards long-term wellness.\r\n\r\n\r\nOur Mind-Body Health Assessment Process\r\n\r\nA lot of people see a variety of doctors for stomach pain, headaches, tiredness or trouble sleeping or for recurring physical problems. Although medical evaluation is critical to determine physical causes, emotional wellbeing, lifestyle habits and chronic stress can also affect the experience and coping of these symptoms. [1][2]\r\n\r\nAt Manovaidya, we believe that understanding the whole person—not just isolated symptoms—provides a more complete picture of health.\r\n\r\nThe assessment process is tailored to the understanding of the connection between emotional wellbeing, lifestyle and physical health, in order to suggest the individual guidance.\r\n\r\n\r\nStep 1 – Understanding Your Health Journey\r\n\r\nEvery consultation begins with listening carefully to your experiences.\r\n\r\nWe discuss:\r\n\r\n•\tYour current physical concerns\r\n•\tEmotional wellbeing\r\n•\tStress levels\r\n•\tSleep quality\r\n•\tDigestive health\r\n•\tLifestyle habits\r\n•\tMedical history\r\n•\tExisting medical conditions\r\n•\tPrevious treatments and investigations\r\n\r\nKnowing how physical and emotional well being work together will give you a greater understanding of well being.\r\n\r\n\r\nStep 2 – Comprehensive Mind-Body Assessment\r\n\r\nThe structured assessment will be looking at a range of factors that might impact on overall wellbeing.\r\n\r\nThese include:\r\n\r\n•\tStress and emotional wellbeing\r\n•\tSleep quality\r\n•\tLifestyle habits\r\n•\tEnergy levels\r\n•\tDigestive wellbeing\r\n•\tEmotional resilience\r\n•\tDaily routine\r\n•\tWork-life balance\r\n•\tBehavioural patterns\r\n•\tOverall quality of life\r\n\r\nThe holistic evaluation helps to uncover any patterns which may be affecting emotional and physical health.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nStep 3 – Understanding Your Mind-Body Wellbeing Profile\r\n\r\nFollowing assessment, our observations are clearly explained in a practical way.\r\n\r\nThis includes:\r\n\r\n•\tEmotional wellbeing\r\n•\tLifestyle influences\r\n•\tStress patterns\r\n•\tDaily routine assessment\r\n•\tAreas needing attention\r\n•\tPersonalised recommendations\r\n•\tPractical next steps\r\n\r\nWe want people to have a better awareness of how emotional wellbeing and lifestyle can impact on their health and to make informed choices about health care.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThe Neuro-Ayurveda Development System\r\n\r\nMind-body health is defined at Manovaidya through the Neuro-Ayurveda Development System, which is a five-pillar system, looking at emotional wellbeing, brain function, health of the gut, behaviour and lifestyle in an integrated way.\r\n\r\nThis is not just looking at physical symptoms or emotional well-being in isolation, but rather it is a way to understand how different systems within the body can support each other to have overall wellness.\r\n\r\n1. Brain Nourishment System\r\n\r\nHealthy brain function influences:\r\n\r\n•\tEmotional regulation\r\n•\tStress resilience\r\n•\tConcentration\r\n•\tMemory\r\n•\tSleep\r\n•\tOverall mental wellbeing\r\n\r\nProtecting your brain health is key to emotional and physical well-being. [1][2]\r\n\r\n\r\n2. Gut Response System\r\n\r\nGut and brain constantly communicate via the gut-brain axis. [4][9]\r\n\r\nThis pillar is about learning how to understand:\r\n\r\n•\tDigestive wellbeing\r\n•\tNutrition\r\n•\tHealthy eating habits\r\n•\tGut health\r\n•\tLifestyle factors that support overall wellness\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n3. Neural Network System\r\n\r\nThe brain is always changing via learning and experience.\r\n\r\nThis pillar is about:\r\n\r\n•\tHealthy thinking patterns\r\n•\tEmotional adaptability\r\n•\tCognitive flexibility\r\n•\tStress resilience\r\n•\tBehavioural awareness\r\n\r\n4. Sensory Integration System\r\n\r\nEmotional and physical health can be affected by daily experiences and by environmental stress.\r\n\r\nThis pillar considers:\r\n\r\n•\tEnvironmental stressors\r\n•\tLifestyle patterns\r\n•\tSensory responses\r\n•\tRelaxation and recovery\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n5. Behaviour Guidance System\r\n\r\nLifestyle behaviours and patterns affect long-term wellbeing.\r\n\r\nThis pillar helps individuals:\r\n\r\n•\tUnderstand stress responses\r\n•\tBuild healthier routines\r\n•\tImprove coping strategies\r\n•\tDevelop sustainable lifestyle habits\r\n\r\n\r\nHow we support Mind-Body Health\r\n\r\nHealth is unique for each person.\r\n\r\nWe take a personal approach to our approach at Manovaidya that will be tailored to each individual's emotional state, physical health concerns and lifestyle.\r\n\r\nSupport may include:\r\n\r\n•\tMind-Body Health Assessment\r\n•\tStress & Lifestyle Assessment\r\n•\tEmotional Wellbeing Guidance\r\n•\tHealthy Routine Planning\r\n•\tNutrition & Lifestyle Education\r\n•\tStress Management Strategies\r\n•\tMind-Body Balance Guidance\r\n•\tProgress Monitoring & Follow-up\r\n\r\nWe want everyone to have a clearer understanding of the link between emotional wellbeing and physical health and encourage healthier habits that will benefit longterm health.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nWhy People Across India Choose Manovaidya\r\n\r\nFor emotional and physical wellbeing, people and families from Delhi, Noida, Gurgaon, Faridabad, Ghaziabad and all over India choose Manovaidya.\r\n\r\nPeople choose us because we focus on:\r\n\r\nComprehensive Mind-Body Health Assessments\r\nNeuro-Ayurveda Development System\r\nGut-Brain Axis Understanding\r\nLifestyle & Stress Management Guidance\r\nHolistic Emotional Wellbeing Support\r\nOnline & In-Clinic Consultations\r\nLong-Term Wellness Approach\r\n\r\nThe focus will be on helping people to improve their emotional health and wellbeing, understand how it can impact on their lifestyle and physical health, and learn to support healthy living every day.\r\n\r\n\r\nAbout Dr. Ankush Garg\r\n\r\nMental Health Specialist & Founder of Manovaidya\r\n\r\nDr. Ankush Garg is the Founder of Manovaidya and the developer of the Neuro-Ayurveda Development System.\r\n\r\nHis work focuses on understanding the relationship between emotional wellbeing, brain health, gut health and lifestyle while helping individuals experiencing stress-related physical symptoms and emotional challenges.\r\n\r\nThrough structured assessments, personalised guidance and continuous follow-up, Dr. Ankush Garg helps individuals better understand the mind-body connection and build healthier long-term wellbeing.\r\n\r\nBased in Delhi NCR, he provides Mind-Body Health consultations for individuals across India through both online and in-clinic appointments.\r\n\r\n\r\nBook a Mind-Body Health Assessment\r\n\r\nAre Stress and Physical Symptoms Affecting Your Daily Life?\r\n\r\nIf you are experiencing recurring digestive discomfort, headaches, fatigue, sleep problems or other physical symptoms alongside ongoing stress or emotional challenges, understanding the relationship between mind and body may help you take a more informed approach to your health. [1][2][10]\r\n\r\nAt Manovaidya, we provide structured Mind-Body Health Assessments, personalised guidance and holistic support through the Neuro-Ayurveda Development System.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nTake a Whole-Person Approach to Your Health\r\n\r\nGood health is not only about treating symptoms—it is also about understanding the relationship between the brain, body, lifestyle and emotional wellbeing. [1][2]\r\n\r\nWhether your concerns involve stress-related digestive issues, headaches, fatigue, sleep disturbances or overall mind-body balance, our team is here to help you better understand your health and support your journey towards long-term wellbeing.\r\n\r\nBook Your Mind-Body Health Assessment Today\r\n\r\n📞 Book Consultation\r\n📞 Talk to Our Team\r\n📞 Schedule Assessment\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nFrequently Asked Questions (FAQs)\r\n\r\n1. What is mind-body health?\r\n\r\nMind/body health is a holistic approach that recognizes the connection between emotional and physical health. The brain and body are in constant communication via the nervous system, hormones, immune system and gut-brain axis. Emotional and physical well-being go hand in hand and are important for good health and quality of life. [1][4][9]\r\n\r\n\r\n2. Can stress affect physical health?\r\n\r\nYes. Stress can affect various systems in the body, such as digestion, sleep, muscle tension, heart rate and emotional health. But not all physical symptoms are due to stress. If symptoms continue or are severe, medical evaluation should always be provided to rule out underlying health conditions. [1][2]\r\n\r\n\r\n3. What is the gut-brain connection?\r\n\r\nGut-brain axis or the gut-brain connection is a bidirectional pathway of communication between the gut and the brain. Some people may find that digestion symptoms can affect their emotional health and wellbeing, and some people may find that their emotional health and wellbeing can affect their digestion. [4][9]\r\n\r\n\r\n4. Can emotional stress affect digestion?\r\n\r\nEmotional stress can cause digestive symptoms for some people, including bloating, indigestion or an increase or decrease in appetite or bowel movements. Digestive symptoms can be caused by so many different things that it is important to be medically evaluated in order to find out the cause. [3][4][10]\r\n\r\n\r\n5. Can stress trigger headaches or migraines?\r\n\r\nStress is known to be a common migraine headache trigger for certain individuals. But there can be several causes for headaches and migraines, so if they are persistent or painful it is always best to investigate the cause by a qualified health care professional. [6]\r\n\r\n\r\n6. Can stress affect blood pressure?\r\n\r\nStress can trigger a temporary rise in blood pressure as the body's stress response. There are lots of factors that affect long-term blood pressure, such as genes, what one eats, exercise, medical and lifestyle factors. Always consult a doctor to assess and treat high blood pressure. [1][5]\r\n\r\n7. Can stress affect thyroid health?\r\n\r\nStress can impact the overall health and wellbeing, as well as the way some people manage to experience symptoms when dealing with thyroid disorders. But, stress is not a substitute for appropriate medical evaluation, diagnosis or treatment of thyroid conditions.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n8. Can emotional wellbeing influence energy levels?\r\n\r\nYes. Energy levels may be affected by emotional stress, sleep, lifestyle habits and physical health. Chronic fatigue can be caused by a variety of factors, and should not be attributed to stress alone. [1][2]\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n9. What are common signs that stress may be affecting physical health?\r\n\r\nSome people notice digestive discomfort, headaches, muscle tension, fatigue, sleep disturbances, changes in appetite or difficulty concentrating during periods of prolonged stress. These symptoms are not specific to stress and should be professionally evaluated if they persist. [1][2][10]\r\n\r\n\r\n10. What is a mind-body health assessment?\r\n\r\nMind-body health assessment is an in-depth assessment of emotional wellbeing, stress, lifestyle, sleep, gastrointestinal issues, and general health and wellbeing. The assessment will be used to identify patterns that could impact wellbeing and inform personalised recommendations.\r\n\r\n\r\n11. How does Manovaidya support mind-body health?\r\n\r\nAt Manovaidya, we start by looking at the whole picture of the emotional wellbeing, lifestyle and physical health and not just the symptoms. Structured assessments, personalised guidance and the Neuro-Ayurveda Development System can aid individuals gain insight into their holistic mental, physical and emotional health.\r\n\r\n\r\n12. What is the Neuro-Ayurveda Development System?\r\n\r\nIn the Neuro-Ayurveda Development System, Manovaidya has developed a structured 5 pillar system to take care of Brain Nourishment, Gut Response, Neural Network Development, Sensory Integration and Behaviour Guidance, and understands the emotional wellbeing, lifestyle and physical health. It promotes a holistic approach and in-depth assessment and individual guidance.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n13. How can I support my mind-body health naturally?\r\n\r\nOverall, good sleep, a healthy diet, exercise, stress management, relaxation, meaningful relationships and healthy daily habits can help contribute to mind-body wellbeing. These measures are in addition to and not as a replacement for appropriate medical care if a health condition exists. [2]\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n14. When should I seek immediate medical attention?\r\n\r\nIf you have severe chest pain or shortness of breath or sudden weakness, stroke-like symptoms, loss of consciousness, or seizures, or if you have any other medical emergency, get medical help right away. Emergency care should not be barred.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n15. Why should I choose Manovaidya for mind-body health care?\r\n\r\nWe understand the whole picture of emotional well being, lifestyle and physical health at Manovaidya through structured evaluations, individual guidance and the Neuro-Ayurveda Development System. We focus on brain health, gut health, stress management and healthy lifestyle habits to promote long-term wellness in the mind/body.\r\n\r\n\r\nReferences\r\n\r\n\r\n1. American Psychological Association (APA) – Stress Effects on the Body\r\nhttps://www.apa.org/topics/stress/body\r\n2. National Center for Complementary and Integrative Health (NCCIH) – Stress\r\nhttps://www.nccih.nih.gov/health/stress\r\n3. National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases (NIDDK) – Irritable Bowel Syndrome (IBS)\r\nhttps://www.niddk.nih.gov/health-information/digestive-diseases/irritable-bowel-syndrome\r\n4. Johns Hopkins Medicine – The Brain-Gut Connection\r\nhttps://www.hopkinsmedicine.org/health/wellness-and-prevention/the-brain-gut-connection\r\n5. World Health Organization (WHO) – Hypertension\r\nhttps://www.who.int/news-room/fact-sheets/detail/hypertension\r\n6. National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke (NINDS) – Migraine\r\nhttps://www.ninds.nih.gov/health-information/disorders/migraine\r\n7. Central Council for Research in Ayurvedic Sciences (CCRAS) – Ministry of AYUSH\r\nhttps://ccras.nic.in/\r\n8. Ministry of AYUSH, Government of India – Ayurveda\r\nhttps://ayush.gov.in/\r\n9. PubMed – The Microbiota-Gut-Brain Axis\r\nhttps://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31460832/\r\n10. PubMed – Stress and the Gut: Pathophysiology, Clinical Consequences and Diagnostic Approach\r\nhttps://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/22314561/\r\nvidIQ";

